        "text": "A few years later, I joined a local group that counts bats. Our new volunteers sometimes arrive with expensive cameras, but they soon find they don't need them. A small torch is useful for finding your way, though. At first I thought a blue filter would do, but our trainer said no, use a red filter. That gives you enough light to see the path without disturbing the bats. We also advise people to wear comfortable shoes because we walk quite a distance."
